# Form dialogs

This is a hard constraint for every add or edit dialog. Do not relax it for one screen, a short form, or a mobile-only tweak.

- Use `Dialog`, `DialogContent`, `DialogHeader`, `DialogBody`, and `DialogFooter` from `src/components/ui/dialog.tsx`. Do not build a second modal.
- `DialogContent` stays viewport-capped. Pass `overflow-hidden` so the card cannot grow past the visual viewport (`h-dvh` / visual-viewport height, `max-h-full`). Width stays `w-full` with a larger-screen cap such as `sm:max-w-lg`.
- Fields live in `DialogBody` (`min-h-0`, `overflow-y-auto`, `overscroll-contain`). That body is the only scroller.
- `DialogHeader` (title) and `DialogFooter` (actions) stay `shrink-0`. They remain visible while the fields scroll. Do not put the title or actions inside the scrolling body.
- Keep `lockDialogScroll` in `dialog.tsx`. Opening a dialog pins `main` and the window. Focusing a field, or the on-screen keyboard resizing the visual viewport, must not jump the list behind the dialog.
- Do not remove the visual-viewport sizing, the focus reveal inside `DialogBody`, or the scroll pin to "simplify" the dialog.
- Do not change theme colors in `src/app/globals.css` to fix dialog layout.

## Atrium form sheet

Copy `src/app/(app)/clients/client-form-dialog.tsx` (mockups d26 and m27).

- On phones `DialogContent` is a bottom sheet (grab handle, `rounded-sheet`, slides up). On desktop it is a centered glass dialog. Do not swap in a different modal or drawer for phones.
- Pass `mobileLayout="nav"` when the footer holds exactly Cancel and Save. Phones then place them beside the title like an iOS sheet. Keep the default `stack` layout for any other footer.
- Long side panels (the access editor, d23 and m24) use `variant="drawer"`.
- Put the fields in one `<FieldGroup layout="inset">` inside `DialogBody`: a grouped list on phones, and a two-column grid from `md:` up. `<Field span="half">` shares a desktop row. Mark errors with `data-invalid` on `Field`, `aria-invalid` on the control, and `FieldError`.
- Every control sets its keyboard and autofill hints (`type`, `inputMode`, `autoComplete`, `autoCapitalize`, `enterKeyHint`). Inputs stay 16px on phones.
- Deletes are not form dialogs. Use `DeleteConfirmDialog`, which keeps the slide-to-delete confirmation.
